+# Graphify
+
+Graphify is available through the AI dev shell for building a local graph of
+this NixOS config repo.
+
+## Backend
+
+This repo does not use Ollama for Graphify. The local backend is `llama-swap`
+running `llama.cpp` on `yifuwuqi`, exposed as an OpenAI-compatible API.
+The wrapper assumes `yifuwuqi` is the service host and reads that host's
+Tailscale address from `modules/addresses.nix`; it uses localhost when running
+on `yifuwuqi` and the derived Tailscale address from other hosts.
+
+That matches the `local` OpenCode provider in `users/programs/opencode.nix`.
+The wrapper also exports Nix's GCC runtime library path before calling `uv`,
+so PyPI wheels such as NumPy can load `libstdc++.so.6` on NixOS.
+Graphify's upstream `openai` backend hardcodes the public OpenAI URL, so the
+wrapper patches that backend to `OPENAI_BASE_URL` before running extraction.
+
+Model names are listed from `modules/services/ai/models.nix`. The wrapper uses
+a configured default model string, and validates both that default and any
+`--model` override against the registry-derived raw model list. The lower token
+budget and single concurrency are intentional for the local `llama.cpp` backend.
+
+## Implementation
+
+The flake shell wiring lives in `nix/devshells/ai.nix`. The `graphify-nix`
+command itself is a rendered shell template in
+`nix/devshells/graphify-nix.sh`. `nix/devshell.nix` only imports the AI shell
+module and keeps the default/sandbox shells separate.
+
+List available raw model names:
+
+```sh
+graphify-nix --list-models
+```
+
+Use one model for a run:
+
+```sh
+graphify-nix --model <model>
+```
+
+## Commands
+
+Enter the shell:
+
+```sh
+nix develop .#ai
+```
+
+Prepare the Nix-only corpus without calling the model:
+
+```sh
+graphify-nix --prepare-only
+```
+
+Build the graph:
+
+```sh
+graphify-nix
+```
+
+Query an existing graph:
+
+```sh
+uv run --with "graphifyy[openai]" graphify query "how do the AI services connect?" --graph graphify-out/graph.json
+```
+
+`graphify-nix` copies `*.nix` files into `.graphify-nix-corpus/` as Markdown
+wrappers, then runs Graphify against that corpus. Generated graph state stays
+local in `graphify-out/`, `.graphify/`, and `.graphify-nix-corpus/`.
